   <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,615.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,615.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,615.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,615.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,613.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,615.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,620.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,617.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Hormuz Tanker Traffic Stays Weak Despite Trump's Peace Claims\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Only three oil tankers transited the Strait of Hormuz on Monday, down from seven vessels recorded on Sunday. In the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, 12 tankers made the crossing, with most vessels keeping their transponders switched on. The subdued shipping activity suggests that concerns over security in the region continue to outweigh optimism generated by Trump's comments.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/hormuz-tanker-traffic-stays-weak-despite-trumps-peace-claims\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery Weighs Fuel Price Review as Market Conditions Shift — Sources\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery is considering a review of its petrol and diesel prices as it evaluates prevailing market conditions. The development comes as international crude oil prices continue to soften.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-weighs-fuel-price-review-as-market-conditions-shift-sources\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria Targets End to Crude Exports as Local Refining Capacity Surges\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has unveiled plans to gradually phase out crude oil exports as Nigeria ramps up domestic refining capacity. The Chief Executive of the Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority, Rabiu Umar, disclosed the strategy on Monday. He said the country’s expanding refining infrastructure, driven by large-scale private investments and modular refineries, could transform Nigeria into Africa's leading refining hub.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigeria-targets-end-to-crude-exports-as-local-refining-capacity-surges\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Climb as Iran Denies Talks with U.S\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude futures climbed above $85 per barrel after tumbling more than seven per cent on Monday. WTI crude also recovered above the $81 mark. Monday's sell-off followed Trump's announcement that he had suspended another planned military strike against Iran. Iran's Foreign Ministry quickly rejected the claim.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-climb-as-iran-denies-talks-with-us\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Trump Pressures Oil Giants to Slash Fuel Prices as Crude Crashes 5%\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    U.S. President Donald Trump has called on American oil companies to immediately reduce retail fuel prices. Crude benchmarks tumbled sharply following his decision to suspend another planned military strike on Iran. Trump also singled out Chevron Chief Executive Officer Mike Wirth.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/trump-pressures-oil-giants-to-slash-fuel-prices-as-crude-crashes-5\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
